Z||000000||Lizzy||11-11-2001||12:49 PM||||Hello everyone.  I bought my daughter her first car at the beginning of the summer.  Of course I chose a Fiero. After a lot of hard work on it we finally got it back from the local bodyshop yesterday.  Just in time for my daughter's birthday tomorrow.  It's an '87 that we kept the original blue, 4cyl, 4 speed.  It has SE on the quarter window, but has a GT front facia and rear spoiler.  Was this a sport model? Or was it ordered that way special in '87?  Curious to know.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lauren'sfiero.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Phil||11-11-2001||12:53 PM||||SE's could be ordered that way- nice car.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">     <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||11-11-2001||12:55 PM||||Looks nice!  The '87 SE came with that front fascia.  Part of the "SE".  I'm guessing the wing was also ordered with it.  It's not standard on them, as you could also have gotten a luggage rack.  Nice though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Smoooooth GT||11-11-2001||01:00 PM||||Love that car...  ohh, Can I call you Daddy?? My b-day is in August, so you have alot of time to get me one too..  lol  Steve<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Smooooth_Yellow_sig_3.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig_blue_3.gif">  <BR>Shaved door hanles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||11-11-2001||01:03 PM||||According to Mark Corbin's "Fiero Spotter's Guide"  You may have a limited poduction model.  There were only 1,401 4 cylinder 87 SEs made and yours is blue another limited paint color only offered in 1987.<P>But his guide also says that 4 speed transmissions were NA, all had 5 speed manual.  RPO code MM4=4 speed,  MM5= 5 speed.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 11-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Lizzy||11-11-2001||02:08 PM||||Thanks for the info.  My typo error, it does have a 5 speed.  Another question, I got a new headliner kit from the Fiero Store.  How do you get the plastic trim off around the doors without breaking it?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Heretic||11-11-2001||03:08 PM||||I've always liked blue. Now , if i could only get my parents to get me a T-TOP Formula for my 16th Birthday..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_1.jpg">      <BR>Word of the week:"Circular"||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroBUZZ||11-11-2001||03:55 PM||||What a great 16th birthday gift!!! Love the blue colour.  <BR>The panels have a few clips in the middle. I find it easier to take em all off starting with the bottom one.  Some of the clips may break (old and brittle) but if you take your time it's pretty simple. Up here in the Great White North the seat belt bolts can be tough.<BR>Put a coat of 'glass resin on the headliner board to strengthen it while it's out.  The old glue and foam will brush off the board easily.<BR>Gary<BR>86 GT<BR>86 SE project<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000008||Nashco||11-11-2001||04:29 PM||||A WHOLE CAR for a birthday present!!!  Geez, must be nice.  I already got my car before I was 16...so my parents were nice enough to let me get my license when I turned 16.  Hmmm, maybe I should have done it the other way..they buy a car, I get the license? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  That's an awesome gift, I'm sure she likes it!  If not, my birthday is coming up here in January...keep me in mind <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
